description:
RD ALFA Microelectronics has 50 years of experience designing and producing HiRel, RadHard & ITAR free for EU, analogue Integrated Circuits (ICs) for aerospace and industrial, including automotive and special purpose microcircuits. Initially founded in 1962, the company is a pioneer in electronics and has regularly participated in European Space Agency (ESA) projects since 2015. RD ALFA Microelectronics Quality Management System (QMS) conforms to the requirements of the International Standard ISO 9001:2015 (confirmed by the Certificate CV20/0092, SGS (Société Générale de Surveillance, Zurich).
 TECHNOLOGIES AND COMPETENCES
 Factory specialists have expertise in analog and analog-to-digital technology (Bi-polar (Bi), Bi-FET, complementary Bi, CMOS, and Bi-CMOS) as well as the design and testing of microcircuits. RD ALFA Microelectronics has developed Quad Operational Amplifier aRD124A that successfully qualified for usage in ESA space missions. 
PRODUCTS AND SERVICES IN SPACE 
• MIL-STD 1553, monolithic dual transceivers; 
• Operational Amplifiers; 
• Comparators; 
• Analog Switch; 
• Transistor Pair. 
EQUIPMENT

• Assembly equipment of the Integrated Circuits in nitrogen atmosphere according to ESCC 9000;

• Testing equipment of the Integrated Circuits according to ESCC 9000. 

MAJOR SPACE PROJECTS AND ACHIEVEMENTS 
• ESA-PECS, Research and Identification of ICs for application in ESA missions, year 2015; 
• ESA-PECS, Development of QUAD Operational Amplifier IC aRD124A, year 2016; 
• ESA-PECS, Development of QUAD Comparator IC aRD139A, year 2018; 
• ESA-PECS, Qualification of QUAD Operational Amplifier IC aRD124A for use in ESA space applications, year 2019. 
CURRENT AND TARGET PARTNERSHIP 
• RD ALFA Microelectronics works closely with such companies as Thales Alenia Space, Airbus Defence and Space, ALTER TECHNOLOGY, and a sales representative office for Europe in Italy: the company Dimac RED S.p.a. 
• We are looking for partners to team up for collaboration in the development of measurement instruments for proposed applications as well as companies using not only industrial, including automotive and special purpose microcircuits, but rad-hard microelectronics components for their space payloads also.
